TIC Survey: Build Script
Version 0.1 · 13 November 2026 · Companion to the TIC Survey PRD
0. How to use this script
This is a build script you can follow step by step yourself, or paste section by section into an AI coding tool (Cursor, Claude Code, Lovable and similar). Each part is self-contained and ends with a short acceptance check. Build in the order given.
What you are building: a web platform with two user types.
• Creator (staff or researcher): signs in, builds surveys from sign language videos, shares a link, reviews signed answers.
• Respondent (student): opens a link, needs no login and no reading, takes a practice run, then answers the survey in video.
Inferred from your uploads [Assumption]. The hex label for the primary colour was too blurry to read, so I sampled the swatch (#034C58). The secondary swatch is yellow but its label showed the accent value, so I used a matching yellow (#F2BE3A). Please check both against your Figma file. The wireframe screen names (for example Q 4a to Q 4d) are read from a small screenshot, so the recording flow below is my best reading of it.
