6.2 Survey builder behaviour
The builder is a two-column page. The left column is an ordered list of question cards. The right column is a live preview that renders the student view of the selected question.
Each question card contains:
1.  Type selector: Single choice, Multiple choice, Signed answer.
2.  Question video: upload a file or record in the browser (uses the same recorder as section 7). Show a thumbnail and duration. A question cannot be saved without a video.
3.  Options (single and multiple choice only): 2 to 4 option cards, each with its own video and an optional thumbnail. Reordering by drag handles and keyboard arrows.
4.  Internal label: a text note for creators, for example Q3 Do you feel safe at school. Never shown to students.
5.  Required toggle.
Survey-level controls: intro video and closing video (both optional, defaults provided), Preview as student, Publish (validates every question has video and every choice question has at least two options), Copy share link, Close survey.
// src/lib/schema.ts
import { z } from 'zod';

export const optionSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().uuid().optional(),
  videoPath: z.string().min(1),
  thumbPath: z.string().optional(),
  label: z.string().optional(),
});

export const questionSchema = z
  .object({
    id: z.string().uuid().optional(),
    kind: z.enum(['single', 'multi', 'signed']),
    videoPath: z.string().min(1, 'Add a sign language video'),
    label: z.string().optional(),
    required: z.boolean().default(true),
    options: z.array(optionSchema).max(4).default([]),
  })
  .refine((q) => q.kind === 'signed' || q.options.length >= 2, {
    message: 'Choice questions need at least two options',
    path: ['options'],
  });

export type QuestionInput = z.infer<typeof questionSchema>;
