8. API routes and data flow
All three routes run on the server with the Supabase service role key.
Route
Method
Behaviour
/api/respondent/start
POST
Takes the slug, checks the survey is published, creates a sessions row, returns the session id plus the question and option list with signed media URLs.
/api/respondent/upload-url
POST
Takes session id and question id, returns a signed upload URL into response-videos/{session}/{question}.webm.
/api/respondent/submit
POST
Takes session id and answers, validates required questions, writes responses, marks the session completed.
// src/app/api/respondent/upload-url/route.ts
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js';
import { z } from 'zod';

const body = z.object({ sessionId: z.string().uuid(), questionId: z.string().uuid() });

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const parsed = body.safeParse(await req.json());
  if (!parsed.success) return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Bad request' }, { status: 400 });

  const db = createClient(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!, process.env.SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY!);
  const { data: session } = await db.from('sessions').select('id,status').eq('id', parsed.data.sessionId).single();
  if (!session || session.status !== 'in_progress') return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Invalid session' }, { status: 403 });

  const path = `${parsed.data.sessionId}/${parsed.data.questionId}.webm`;
  const { data, error } = await db.storage.from('response-videos').createSignedUploadUrl(path);
  if (error) return NextResponse.json({ error: error.message }, { status: 500 });
  return NextResponse.json({ path, ...data });
}
9. Offline and reliability
Schools may have poor connectivity, so the respondent experience must tolerate it.
1.  Register a service worker (Serwist) that precaches the respondent shell and runtime-caches survey videos once a survey has been started.
2.  Keep answers and recorded blobs in IndexedDB with idb-keyval, keyed by session and question. Never rely on memory alone.
3.  On submit, upload recordings one at a time with retry and exponential back-off. Show a simple visual state (waiting, sending, sent) with icons only.
4.  If the browser goes offline mid-survey, continue normally and show a small offline icon. Sync automatically when the connection returns.
5.  If the tab is closed, resuming the link restores the session and answers from IndexedDB.
// src/lib/offline.ts
import { set, get, del } from 'idb-keyval';

export const saveRecording = (sid: string, qid: string, blob: Blob) => set(`rec:${sid}:${qid}`, blob);
export const loadRecording = (sid: string, qid: string) => get<Blob>(`rec:${sid}:${qid}`);
export const clearRecording = (sid: string, qid: string) => del(`rec:${sid}:${qid}`);

export async function uploadWithRetry(url: string, blob: Blob, tries = 5) {
  for (let i = 0; i < tries; i++) {
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, { method: 'PUT', body: blob, headers: { 'Content-Type': blob.type } });
      if (res.ok) return true;
    } catch { /* offline, retry */ }
    await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 1000 * 2 ** i));
  }
  return false;
}
10. Accessibility, privacy and safety checklist
• Respondent screens use no required reading. Any text is secondary and optional.
• Every interactive element is keyboard reachable and has an accessible name (for the benefit of facilitators and creators).
• Contrast meets WCAG 2.2 AA. Teal on white and white on teal both pass, but check yellow text on white (it fails, so use yellow only as a fill with dark text).
• Students are never asked for their name, email or any identifier. Sessions are anonymous unless the creator adds cohort codes later.
• Recordings are private, encrypted at rest, and viewable only by creators and reviewers in the owning organisation.
• A facilitator in the room cannot see answers, because the review list shows only to the student.
• Add a written data protection notice and consent step, signed off for Ghana's Data Protection Act, 2012 (Act 843), before real pupils use the product.
